g), covariates x. Define the all-treated / all-control counterparts analytically (f1 = 1 if deg>0 else 0, s1 = deg, f2 = 1 if two-hop walks exist else 0).\",\n    \"Write def candidate_designs(...) returning a dict of named model specs, each a function mapping (z or all-treated flag) to a design matrix: M0 linear fraction (the baseline); M1 count (s1 / mean degree) replacing the fraction; M2 fraction + two-hop fraction; M3 fraction + own x log1p(deg) + own x x_j + frac x log1p(deg); M4 saturating shape 1-exp(-k f1) for k in {1,3,8}; M5 smooth threshold sigmoid((f1-t)/0.1) for t in {0.25,0.5,0.75}; M6 saturating count 1-exp(-s1/(k*median_deg)) for k in {0.5,1,2}. All are fit by OLS (np.linalg.lstsq) so runtime stays well under the 2.5 s soft budget on\n    \"Write def bic_gate(...): compute BIC = n*log(RSS/n) + p*log(n) for each candidate; adopt a non-baseline model only if BIC(M0) - BIC(model) > 10 (strong evidence); among those passing take BIC weights (softmax of -0.5*BIC difference) to average the GATE estimates; if none pass return the M0 estimate exactly.\",\n    \"Add a sanity guard: if the selected/averaged estimate differs from the M0 estimate by more than 3*max(|est0|, se0), or any prediction is non-finite, fall back to M0; also winsorise the all-treated feature values to at most the 99.5th percentile of observed-exposure feature values times 3 for count-type features.\",\n    \"Write def sandwich_se(...): HC1 sandwich delta-method standard error of the contrast vector for the chosen model (for averages, use weight-mixed se plus the between-model spread); report ci_low/ci_high = estimate -/+ (1.96*se + |estimate - est0|) so the interval widens when the gate switches away from linear, and enforce ci_low <= estimate <= ci_high.\",\n    \"Do not add any diagnostics to the response beyond the three required keys (keep the response minimal); do not use time-dependent or unseeded randomness.\",\n    \"Self-check by reading code paths only (no execution is possibl